gs to the pet salon last Friday, noting they looked cute with shiny coats, behaved well, and were happy and safe.\n  - My dogs: Audrey's dogs enjoy meeting new people. They recently had grooming and look soft and fluffy.\n  - Pixie: Pixie is one of Audrey's four dogs, a Chihuahua mix, who curls up in her own bed to relax. Audrey is busy giving attention to her four dogs.\n  - mountain life: Audrey recalls a special, peaceful moment by a gorgeous mountain lake with friends, characterized by the sound of birds, still water, and fresh air. She notes that regular grooming keeps her companions looking good.\n  - doggie playdate: Audrey recently organized a doggy playdate with neighbors' dogs, noting the sweet sight of wagging tails, which followed a previous playdate last Friday with her three 3-year-old dogs.\n  - four pups: Audrey's four pups enjoy many activities, including puzzles, training, and hide-and-seek. Audrey meets with a dog owners group weekly for tips and playdates.\n  - puppies and dogs: Audrey has four doggies that she takes care of to keep them happy and healthy. Andrew mentioned he would not want puppies and dogs to be punished.\n  - doggo: Audrey groomed her dogs, who looked cute with shiny coats after being good at the salon. Andrew adopted another dog and shared a photo.\n  - dogs: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon; they looked cute, groomed, and had shiny coats. Andrew has two dogs, Toby and Buddy. They are considered family members.\n  - her pups: One of Audrey's pups pulled so hard on the leash last Friday at the park that it busted; she chased and caught the pup. Audrey calmed her by petting, hugging, and speaking calmly.\n  - other pups: The dogs of Audrey love Fetch and Frisbee and enjoy running around and meeting other pups, who they could keep running with for hours.\n  - furry friend: Audrey took her furry kids to the pet salon last Friday where they were groomed, looked cute with shiny coats, and behaved well. Andrew considers his dogs