nated from a trip to Banff. (event_time: 2023-12-09T13:45:00Z)\n  - Sam cannot feel the same way about Love as Evan seems to. (event_time: 2023-12-26T16:25:00Z)\n  - Evan asks Sam how Sam has been feeling lately. (event_time: 2023-08-15T16:20:00Z)\n  - Evan considers Sam a person to talk to. (event_time: 2023-11-09T21:13:00Z)\n  - Sam asked Evan about the relaxing nature of the trip to Jasper. (event_time: 2023-05-24T19:11:00Z)\n</FACTS>\n\n# These are the most relevant entities\n# ENTITY_NAME: entity summary\n<ENTITIES>\n  - Evan: Evan expressed being in love at first sight with a woman from Canada, feeling a spark and believing in their connection.\n  - SO: Evan met a Canadian woman referred to as his 'new SO' during a trip to Canada; being with her makes him feel alive, and they enjoyed hiking and biking together.\n  - woman from Canada: Evan is in love with the woman from Canada, stating he was in love with her at first sight and questioning why they hadn't married sooner.\n  - Evan: Evan told Sam he is in love with a woman from Canada, whom he married, and expressed joy from viewing a painting that helped him recognize his feelings.\n  - Evan: Evan got married last week to the woman from Canada, whom he loved at first sight. He confirmed his love at first sight feeling to Sam.\n  - Love: Evan expressed being in love at first sight with a woman from Canada, stating he regrets not marrying her sooner.\n  - Evan: Evan told Sam he is in love at first sight with a woman from Canada and expressed regret for not marrying her sooner.\n  - Evan: Evan told Sam he is in love with a woman, possibly from Canada, and they did not marry sooner.\n  - Canadian woman: Evan met an awesome Canadian woman in Canada last week. Being with her is fun, energizing, and makes him feel alive, offering a nice change after dealing with health issues.\n  - spark: Evan felt a spark inside when he saw the woman from Canada, which made him feel like time stopped and that it was so right.\n  - Evan: Evan is motivated by adventure on interesting hikes. Last week, he went on a trip to Canada and met an incredible Canadian woman who makes him feel alive.\n  - Sam: Sam congratulated Evan, asked if a woman mentioned was from Canada, and commented that art is amazing at expressing emotions.\n  - Sam: Sam congratulated Evan on his relationship and asked if he believes in love at first sight after learning Evan was in love with the woman from Canada at first sight.\n  - Evan: Evan married his partner last week. Evan was asked by Sam if his spouse is the woman from Canada. Evan had previously mentioned enjoying books, painting, driving, and hiking.\n  - Sam: Sam greeted Evan, congratulated him, asked about a woman from Canada, and jokingly suggested putting a GPS sensor on Evan's keys.\n  - Sam: Sam greeted Evan, congratulated him on getting married last week, and asked if his spouse was the woman from Canada.\n  - Evan: Evan told his extended family about his marriage and plans to try poutine in Canada next month. He told Sam he had too much to drink last night and did something regrettable involving roses.\n  - innermost thoughts and feelings: Evan describes needing an outlet to express innermost thoughts and feelings to figure things out and make sense of them.\n  - Canada: Evan and his partner are going to Canada next month for their honeymoon to explore snowy landscapes. Sam mentioned something is a Canadian thing.\n  - someone who gets Evan: Evan's partner is someone who gets Evan, and Evan feels lucky to have found them. Evan and their partner announced their marriage to their extended family.\n  - Evan: Evan greeted Sam, mentioned taking the Prius for a mountain drive last weekend, and was in a minor accident on the way back. He also shared he got married last week.\n  - Evan: Evan told Sam that his partner was not thrilled but understood an accident involving rose bushes; he plans to be more careful and enjoys small moments outdoors.\n  - feelings: Evan experiences a massive rush of joy from a painting, using art to recognize and handle feelings. Sam expresses themself through writing to sort out feelings.\n  - Evan: Evan informed their extended family about their marriage, receiving a lot of love and support. Evan feels lucky and that their families' happiness is the best part.\n  - Evan: Evan's partner was not thrilled but understood an accident involving rose bushes; he was also encouraged by Sam about controlling dreams.\n  - Evan: Evan congratulated Sam on becoming a Weight Watchers coach. Evan shared a picture taken last Friday at a favorite beach spot where he watches waves and sunsets to find peace.\n  - Evan: Evan is excited as his partner is pregnant. He looks forward to parenthood, remembering the joy of his first child, and is planning a family reunion next summer.\n  - Evan: Evan mentioned his son had an accident last Tuesday after falling off his bike and is now doing better. He recently finished a contemporary figurative painting emphasizing emotional state.\n  - Evan: Evan enjoyed skiing, noting the amazing snow and plans to return next year. Evan also captures the tranquil beauty of nature in paintings.\n  - Evan: Evan mentioned a minor accident that dampened telling work friends about getting married; they have been very supportive.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2091,"context_chars":8214,"retrieval_duration":0.2390298843383789,"response_duration":2.653026819229126,"total_duration":2.892056703567505,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer captures the essence of Evan's feelings and descriptions of the woman, mentioning that he feels alive around her and that their moments together are fun and energizing, which aligns with the gold answer.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides all the necessary information to answer the question about how Evan describes the woman he met in Canada and his feelings for her. It includes details that he finds her cool, incredible, and that being with her makes him feel alive. Additionally, it mentions that every moment with her is fun and energizing, and he feels lucky to have someone who understands him. These elements align perfectly with the golden answer, confirming that the context is complete.","missing_elements":[],"present_elements":["Evan was in love with the woman from Canada at first sight.","Being with the Canadian woman makes Evan feel alive.","Moments with the Canadian woman are fun and energizing for Evan.","Evan feels really lucky to have someone who gets him."]},{"user_id":null,"graph_id":"v2_full_onto_2_experiment_graph_8","test_id":"v2_full_onto_2_graph_8_qa_19","category":"3","difficulty":"unknown","query":"Considering their conversations and personal growth, what advice might Evan and Sam give to someone facing a major life transition or challenge?","golden_answer":"Evan and Sam would likely advise embracing small, consistent changes​​, finding stress-relieving activities like hiking​​, painting, and road trips​​, and the importance of friendship and support in navigating challenges​​.","hypothesis":"Evan and Sam would likely offer the following advice to someone facing a major life transition or challenge:\n\n1. **Take It One Day at a Time**: Evan emphasizes the importance of managing challenges by focusing on daily progress rather than overwhelming oneself with the bigger picture. This approach can help reduce anxiety and make the transition feel more manageable.\n\n2. **Embrace Small Steps**: Both Evan and Sam encourage taking small, manageable steps forward. This can help build confidence and momentum, making it easier to navigate through tough times.\n\n3. **Appreciate the Little Things**: Evan suggests taking time to appreciate the small joys in life, which can provide comfort and positivity during challenging periods. This practice can help shift focus from difficulties to gratitude.\n\n4. **Seek Support**: They would advise reaching out to friends or loved ones for support. Evan and Sam have shown that having someone to talk to can be invaluable during tough times.\n\n5. **Stay Open to New Experiences**: Both encourage trying new things and stepping out of one’s comfort zone. This can lead to personal growth and unexpected opportunities, which can be particularly beneficial during transitions.\n\n6. **Find Enjoyable Activities**: Engaging in activities that bring joy, such as exercise or hobbies, can help alleviate stress and improve overall well-being.\n\n7. **Be Patient with Yourself**: Recognizing that transitions can be difficult and that it’s okay to feel overwhelmed is important. They would likely stress the need for self-compassion during these times.\n\n8. **Focus on Progress, Not Perfection**: They would remind someone that progress is more important than achieving perfection, encouraging a mindset that values growth over immediate results.\n\nBy sharing these insights, Evan and Sam would aim to inspire resilience and positivity in anyone facing significant life changes.","context":"\nFACTS and ENTITIES represent relevant context to the current conversation.\n\n# These are the most relevant facts for the conversation along with the datetime of the event that the fact refers to.\n# If a fact mentions something happening a week ago, then the datetime will be the date time of last week and not the datetime\n# of when the fact was stated.\n# Timestamps in memories represent the actual time the event occurred, not the time the event was mentioned in a message.\n\n<FACTS>\n  - Evan offers encouragement to Sam, stating that Sam can handle tough times. (event_time: 2024-01-11T21:37:00Z)\n  - Evan advises Sam to take things one day at a time (event_time: 2023-12-17T18:48:00Z)\n  - Sam is encouraged by Evan to keep moving forward slowly and taking small steps when feeling overwhelmed. (event_time: 2023-08-15T16:20:00Z)\n  - Evan suggests Sam might find Love in unexpected places by embracing the journey. (even