ir head, and is dealing with movement-limiting discomfort while trying dietary changes.\n  - Evan: Evan congratulated Sam on becoming a Weight Watchers coach. Evan shared a picture taken last Friday at a favorite beach spot where he watches waves and sunsets to find peace.\n  - Evan: Evan congratulated Sam on becoming a Weight Watchers coach, finding it exciting and rewarding.\n  - flexibility: Evan is considering trying yoga for stress relief and flexibility, asking Sam for their opinion on the activity.\n  - Sam: Sam is dealing with rough health issues, feeling weighed down but trying to stay positive. Sam discussed health and rose bush news with Evan.\n  - Evan: Evan greeted Sam, mentioned taking the Prius for a mountain drive last weekend, and was in a minor accident on the way back. He also shared he got married last week.\n  - events: Evan apologized for missing events due to personal challenges and offered support to Sam.\n  - Evan: Evan's partner was not thrilled but understood an accident involving rose bushes; he was also encouraged by Sam about controlling dreams.\n  - Evan: Evan's partner understood an accident; he promised future caution. He was asked about low-impact exercises. Evan offered support to Sam.\n  - Evan: Evan told Sam he is in love with a woman from Canada, whom he married, and expressed joy from viewing a painting that helped him recognize his feelings.\n  - Sam: Sam congratulated Evan on announcing his marriage to his extended family, acknowledged the value of family support, and shared positive sentiments about Evan's bond. Sam also mentioned something being a Canadian thing.\n  - Sam: Sam congratulated Evan on sharing marriage news with family and wished them an incredible honeymoon filled with skiing, local dishes, and breathtaking views.\n  - Sam: Sam is dealing with difficult health issues and a heavy feeling, but is trying to stay positive. Sam found being in nature calming and commented on an amazing picture of a lake.\n  - Sam: Sam is dealing with discomfort limiting movement and is attempting dietary changes. Sam previously expressed excitement about being a coach and plans to hike with Evan.\n  - life: Evan had a recent health scare that was resolved, teaching him the value of life and enjoying the moment. He is feeling fine now.\n  - Sam: Sam congratulated Evan on the exciting news that Evan's partner is pregnant, expressing enthusiasm for parenthood.\n  - Sam: Sam congratulated Evan, asked if a woman mentioned was from Canada, and commented that art is amazing at expressing emotions.\n  - Sam: Sam congratulated Evan on his relationship and asked if he believes in love at first sight after learning Evan was in love with the woman from Canada at first sight.\n  - Evan: Evan mentioned life throws curveballs, is engrossed in a book, and described a location two hours away as worth the drive for its views and atmosphere.\n  - Sam: Sam is aware of Evan's marriage news and offered support. Sam's doctor stated their weight is a serious health risk, prompting plans to eat healthier despite sugary cravings.\n  - Sam: Sam is planning to go on a hike with Evan, described as a fun challenge and an opportunity to appreciate nature.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2008,"context_chars":8090,"retrieval_duration":0.17366504669189453,"response_duration":6.096007585525513,"total_duration":6.269672632217407,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer covers the same themes as the gold answer, including embracing small changes, finding stress-relieving activities, and the importance of support, thus aligning well with the advice Evan and Sam would give.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides all the necessary information to answer the question regarding the advice Evan and Sam might give to someone facing a major life transition or challenge. It includes specific advice about embracing small, consistent changes, taking things one day at a time, finding stress-relieving activities like hiking, and the importance of friendship and support. These elements align perfectly with the golden answer, indicating that the context is comprehensive and sufficient to construct a complete response.","missing_elements":[],"present_elements":["Evan offers encouragement to Sam, stating that Sam can handle tough times.","Evan advises Sam to take things one day at a time.","Sam is encouraged by Evan to keep moving forward slowly and taking small steps when feeling overwhelmed.","Evan suggests Sam might find Love in unexpected places by embracing the journey.","Evan encourages Sam to continue making progress.","Evan suggests to Sam that they should take time to appreciate the little things in life.","Evan encourages Sam to keep trying new things."]},{"user_id":null,"graph_id":"v2_full_onto_2_experiment_graph_3","test_id":"v2_full_onto_2_graph_3_qa_127","category":"4","difficulty":"unknown","query":"What did Joanna write yesterday that appeared on the big screen?","golden_answer":"screenplay bits","hypothesis":"Joanna wrote parts of a screenplay that were shown on the big screen yesterday, which was on June 4, 2022.","context":"\nFACTS and ENTITIES represent relevant context to the current conversation.\n\n# These are the most relevant facts for the conversation along with the datetime of the event that the fact refers to.\n# If a fact mentions something happening a week ago, then the datetime will be the date time of last week and not the datetime\n# of when the fact was stated.\n# Timestamps in memories represent the actual time the event occurred, not the time the event was mentioned in a message.\n\n<FACTS>\n  - Joanna wrote parts of a screenplay that were shown on the big screen the day before the current message. (event_time: 2022-06-04T00:00:00Z)\n  - Joanna saw a movie script that she contributed to shown on the big screen for the first time. (event_time: 2022-10-23T00:00:00Z)\n  - Joanna wrote the characters and dialogue that appeared in the movie script (event_time: 2022-10-25T20:16:00Z)\n  - Nate congratulated Joanna regarding her movie script being shown on the big screen. (event_time: 2022-10-25T20:16:00Z)\n  - Joanna hopes her screenplay ends up on the big screen. (event_time: 2022-02-07T09:27:00Z)\n  - Joanna contributed to a movie script. (event_time: 2022-10-23T00:00:00Z)\n  - Joanna hopes her screenplay gets noticed and makes it to the screen. (event_time: 2022-02-25T13:07:00Z)\n  - Nate hopes that Joanna's screenplay gets put on the big screen. (event_time: 2022-02-07T09:27:00Z)\n  - Joanna is a writer. (event_time: 2022-09-14T13:43:00Z)\n  - Joanna is currently writing a movie script. (event_time: 2022-11-07T20:10:00Z)\n  - Joanna is the author of a published movie. (event_time: 2022-07-10T14:34:00Z)\n  - Joanna engages in writing. (event_time: 2022-01-21T19:31:00Z)\n  - Joanna participated in an audition yesterday (event_time: 2022-03-23T00:00:00Z)\n  - Joanna is finding the recent experience of finishing her script a wild ride. (event_time: 2022-03-18T18:59:00Z)\n  - The audition Joanna had yesterday was for a writing gig (event_time: 2022-03-23T00:00:00Z)\n  - The movie script written by Joanna is a love story. (event_time: 2022-11-07T20:10:00Z)\n  - Joanna experiences inspiration in cool places, suggesting she could write a movie there (event_time: 2022-05-12T15:35:00Z)\n  - Joanna is inspired to write about a thirty year old woman on a journey of self-discovery. (event_time: 2022-02-25T13:07:00Z)\n  - Joanna is inspired to write about self-discovery. (event_time: 2022-02-25T13:07:00Z)\n  - Joanna started writing another screenplay while waiting to hear back about the first one (event_time: 2022-02-25T13:07:00Z)\n  - Writing gives Joanna a chance to put down all her thoughts (event_time: 2022-08-14T18:12:00Z)\n  - Joanna watched the thing for which she wrote the book. (event_time: None)\n  - Joanna finished working on her first full screenplay. (event_time: 2022-01-21T00:00:00Z)\n  - Joanna recently started writing a book. (event_time: 2022-07-10T14:34:00Z)\n  - Joanna uses writing as a way to express her feelings (event_time: 2022-08-14T18:12:00Z)\n  - Joanna feels like she could write a whole movie when she is in cool places (event_time: 2022-05-12T15:35:00Z)\n  - Joanna has been working on a screenplay. (event_time: 2022-05-02T11:54:00Z)\n  - Joanna chose to write about loss because it is personal. (event_time: 2022-05-20T19:49:00Z)\n  - Joanna uses writing to create wild worlds (event_time: 2022-01-23T14:01:00Z)\n  - Joanna cannot stop thinking about the screenplay (event_time: 2022-02-25T13:07:00Z)\n</FACTS>\n\n# These are the most relevant entities\n# ENTITY_NAME: entity summary\n<ENTITIES>\n  - big screen: Joanna is writing a movie script, a love story with challenges, hoping to get it on the big screen.\n  - screenplay: Joanna wrote parts of a screenplay that appeared on the big screen yesterday and submitted a recent screenplay to a film contest.\n  - page: Joanna described seeing characters she wrote jump off the page and become real on the big screen, which was the third time this has happened.\n  - love story: Joanna is writing a movie script for a love story that involves many challenges; she is working hard and hopes to see it on the big screen.\n  - characters and dialogue: Joanna saw characters and dialogue she wrote acted out on the big screen for the third time, describing the experience as amazing and rewarding.\n  - hard work: Joanna found seeing her hard work in writing a movie script acted out on the big screen a surreal and satisfying experience, the third time this has happened.\n  - characters: Joanna saw characters she wrote acted out on the big screen for the third time, finding the experience rewarding. Nate inquired about the character on the left in a shared photo.\n  - director: Joanna hopes a director falls in love with her screenplay to get it on the big screen.\n  - film festivals: Joanna submitted her screenplay to a film festival, feeling relief, excitement, and worry while hoping a producer or director selects it for the big screen.\n  - producer: Joanna hopes a producer or director will like her screenplay enough for it to be shown on the big screen.\n  - identity: Joanna is writing a personal story about loss, identity, and connection which she has had for ages but recently found the courage to write.\n  - writing gig: Joanna had an audition yesterday for a writing gig, feeling a mix of excitement and anxiety afterward. Nate previously encouraged her, noting her hard work and passion.\n  - audition: Joanna had an audition for a writing gig yesterday; she feels mixed emotions but is excited, and Nate wished her luck.\n  - movie script: Joanna is filming a movie based on her road-trip script. She previously hoped for big-screen distribution, and Nate asked about future script submissions.\n  - animals: Nate suggested Joanna write down things her animals like due to Joanna experiencing facial puffiness and itchiness around certain animals, causing avoidance.\n  - hometown: Joanna found an awesome, gorgeous hiking trail in her hometown yesterday, noting nature is inspiring and a great way to reset.\n  - the last one: Joanna is inspired to write a story about a thirty-year-old woman on a self-discovery journey after a loss, similar to 'the last one'.\n  - picture: Nate complimented Joanna's drawings, asking what inspired them. Joanna previously mentioned seeing her writing acted out and Nate complimented a hiking picture.\n  - writing: Joanna feels she cannot stop writing recently, appreciating Nate's support and encouragement.\n  - drama: Joanna felt inspired to write a drama after hiking on amazing trails in her town.\n  - script: Joanna is filming a movie from her road-trip script. An actor praised the script, making Joanna excited and giving her chills.\n  - something delicious: Nate invited Joanna to try something super yummy that he made yesterday.\n  - book: Joanna finished writing and editing her book last week, exploring themes of sisterhood, love, and chasing dreams. The book had previously been shared with her writers group.\n  - seeing all of the characters and dialogue I wrote being acted out: Joanna experienced seeing all of the characters and dialogue she wrote being acted out, which was rewarding and the third time this has happened to her.\n  - Joanna: Joanna is filming her own movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and is excited to show her vision.\n  - Jo: Joanna (Jo) asked Nate if he celebrated good feedback people are connecting with his writing. Previously, she asked about a couple he met while walking Max.\n  - watching movies: Joanna enjoys watching movies as a hobby, in addition to writing, reading, and exploring nature.\n  - movie: Joanna is filming her movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and enjoys showing her vision, with Nate asking about the coolest moment.\n  - writing projects: Joanna is busy with writing projects, which she finds to be the best thing ever, a mix of highs and lows. Writing is an escape, a way to express feelings, and healing.\n  - writers group: Joanna shared her book with her writers group last week and received great feedback. She recently finished a cute little bookmark for one of the ladies at her writing club.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2009,"context_chars":8161,"retrieval_duration":0.15781712532043457,"response_duration":2.2179267406463623,"total_duration":2.375743865966797,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer mentions 'parts of a screenplay' which aligns with the gold answer 'screenplay bits', and it also references the same time frame of 'yesterday', making it correct.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides clear information that Joanna wrote parts of a screenplay that were shown on the big screen yesterday. This directly answers the questi