ing to Nate. Joanna congratulated Nate on his second video game tournament win last week.\n  - Valorant: Nate won the final of a big Valorant tournament last Saturday. He continues to prepare for other tournaments, though Joanna incorrectly assumed it was a Japanese game series.\n  - video games: Nate won a Valorant tournament championship last Saturday, is preparing for others, enjoys 'Xeonoblade Chronicles', and is creating YouTube content for video games.\n  - tournament: Nate's game tournament was pushed back, and he did not make it to the finals. He plans to win the next time.\n  - champion: Nate won a big Valorant tournament final last Saturday, feeling it was the best feeling to see his name as the champion.\n  - gaming tournaments: Nate's game tournament was pushed back. He did not make it to the finals but plans to join a new gaming team after his next tournament.\n  - high scores: Nate is helping friends reset their high scores at the international video game tournament, an activity Joanna encouraged him to continue.\n  - gaming: Nate's game tournament was postponed, and he did not make it to the finals, but he intends to compete again.\n  - Nate: Nate praised Joanna for setting up meetings with movie producers, comparing her success to winning a video game tournament, and expressed pride in her feeling hopeful and inspired.\n  - Street Fighter: Nate is really good at Street Fighter, playing it often with friends, and recently competed in a local tournament for the game.\n  - favorite game: Joanna asked Nate what his favorite game is after he won a Valorant tournament.\n  - Nate: Nate made homemade coconut ice cream with sprinkles. His game tournament was postponed, and he didn't make the finals. He creates YouTube gaming content. He expressed support for Joanna filming her movie.\n  - setback: Nate experienced a setback in a video game tournament after previously winning an international tournament. Joanna expressed sympathy for the setback.\n  - goals: J