hn: John started playing board games, trying \"Dungeons of the Dragon.\" He enjoys electronic and rock music and used to play drums. He left his 3-year IT job for a new one aligned with his values.\n  - John: John is loving sharing his coding journey and tracking everything. He also bought many new books, almost completely filling his bookcase.\n  - John: John started a new startup yesterday focusing on portable smokers and has already welded one from metal.\n  - John: John is working on a cool coding project with his siblings, which is a game to help them learn. He is also working on his first professional website for a small business.\n  - John: John is working on his first professional website project for a local small business and is currently playing AC Valhalla.\n  - John: John collaborated with a game developer to create a unique online board game and ended a conversation with James about it. Previously, he won a chess tournament and organized charity gaming tournaments.\n  - John: John expressed empathy to James about losing power during a game and later asked James about his mother's friend possibly still being in the army.\n  - John: John plays drums, recently chatted with James about a new RPG with a cool story and tough gameplay, which sometimes causes lag and errors.\n  - John: John empathized with James about losing power during a game. John stated a seminar he led went well, featuring a great turnout and knowledge sharing.\n  - John: John is experiencing a mix of emotions, feeling determined and passionate, yet overwhelmed and stressed due to balancing personal and professional life.\n  - John: John hosted a gaming tournament where he and his pals played Fortnite, Overwatch, and Apex Legends to raise money for a children's hospital.\n  - John's siblings: John's siblings signed up for programming and are playing a simple, text-based adventure game to work on coding skills.\n  - John: John started a startup making portable smokers, welding one prototype