y.\n  - career options: Caroline is excited about continuing her education and checking out career options.\n  - my own journey: Caroline shared details of her transgender journey, including struggles and development since coming out and starting transition three years ago, at a school event to inspire others.\n  - next time: Melanie asked Caroline what she hopes to do for the next time, following Caroline's volunteering experience.\n  - friends and community: Caroline noted that Melanie's friends and community really have her back.\n  - adoption journey: Caroline passed adoption agency interviews last Friday, a major step toward her goal of building a family and giving a home to needy kids.\n  - Sweden: Caroline received a special necklace from her grandma in Sweden, which stands for love, faith, and strength, reminding her of her roots and family support.\n  - Melanie: Melanie congratulated Caroline on passing adoption agency interviews, viewing adoption as a loving way to build a family for needy kids, and encouraged Caroline to be herself.\n  - these kids: Caroline is excited to build a family and give a loving, safe home to 'these kids' through adoption, ensuring they experience love and acceptance.\n  - hope: Caroline learned from an LGBTQ conference that tough times don't last, as hope and love exist.\n  - who I really am: Caroline found out who she really is with invaluable help from friends, family, and mentors during tough times, and now wants to pass that support to others.\n  - authenic self-expression: Caroline realized being her authentic self, transitioning, and expressing herself freely with support was the best part of her experience.\n  - supportive community of hope: Caroline aims to build a strong, supportive community of hope by sharing her journey and experiences to promote understanding and acceptance.\n  - transgender journey: Caroline created a plate for a local church reflecting her transgender journey and acceptance of growth and change, e