ing, referencing a past coconut recommendation from Nate.\n  - dairy-free options: Joanna is interested in dairy-free options like coconut or almond milk due to lactose intolerance. Nate wants to share recipes for dairy-free options.\n  - dairy-free: Joanna likes dairy-free desserts, especially those made with almond milk. Nate previously taught vegan ice cream recipes on his cooking show.\n  - cooking show: Nate taught vegan ice cream recipes on his cooking show last Monday, which he enjoyed and used to learn new recipes. Joanna congratulated Nate and expressed interest in watching.\n  - coconut milk icecream: Nate is loving experimenting with flavors and made colorful bowls of coconut milk ice cream. Joanna previously called this ice cream 'so good!'. Nate's existing summary mentions it's smooth, creamy, dairy-free, and vegan.\n  - desserts: Joanna will bring some of her dessert recipes to share with Nate, building on a prior conversation where they discussed dairy-free dessert recipes.\n  - desserts I bake: Joanna has been making all sorts of desserts (cookies, pies, cakes) that suit everyone's diets and will share more recipes with Nate soon. Nate previously made chocolate and vanilla swirl desserts and values Joanna's enjoyment.\n  - lactose intolerant: Joanna is lactose intolerant and is trying dairy-free options like coconut or almond milk, which includes making dairy-free chocolate coconut cupcakes with raspberry frosting.\n  - cake: Nate expressed interest in trying Joanna's chocolate and raspberry cake, building upon a previous compliment about a cake she made and her dessert-making skills.\n  - recipe: Joanna has a tasty recipe she is perfecting; she previously shared a dessert recipe with blueberries, coconut milk, and a gluten-free crust. Nate suggested trying this recipe.\n  - dessert: Joanna shared a dessert recipe made with blueberries, coconut milk, and a gluten-free crust. Nate acknowledged it, saying it looks amazing and he will try it.\n  - dairy-free chocolate coconut cupcakes with raspberry frosting: Joanna made dairy-free chocolate coconut cupcakes with raspberry frosting as a fun challenge while exploring dairy-free options due to her lactose intolerance.\n  - dairy-free [recipe]: Joanna tried her newest dairy-free recipe yesterday, which was a winner with her family. She enjoys mixing and matching flavors.\n  - baking: Joanna is interested in baking treats. Nate expressed eagerness to try Joanna's baking and suggested that baking and cooking bring them together.\n  - dairy-free chocolate cake with raspberries: Joanna likes making a dairy-free chocolate cake with raspberries, describing it as moist, delicious, and perfectly sweet.\n  - recipes: Joanna will bring some of her recipes to share desserts with Nate.\n  - almond milk: Joanna used almond milk last Friday to make a dairy-free dessert that she found delicious, as she avoids dairy.\n  - advice: Joanna gave advice to Nate after his game tournament was pushed back and he didn't make the finals. Nate acknowledged the advice.\n  - dairy-free flavors: Joanna is tempted to try dairy-free flavors after hearing about chocolate and berries options.\n  - ice cream: Joanna thanked Nate for offering mouthwatering ice cream.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2017,"context_chars":8333,"retrieval_duration":0.18858766555786133,"response_duration":2.173635482788086,"total_duration":2.3622231483459473,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer accurately reflects the gold answer by mentioning both dairy-free margarine and coconut oil as substitutes for butter in dairy-free baking.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides all necessary information to answer the question about what substitution Nate suggests for butter in dairy-free baking. It explicitly states that dairy-free margarine and coconut oil can be used as substitutes for butter, which aligns perfectly with the golden answer.","missing_elements":[],"present_e